clean_summary:
Very impressive! Congrats to @GoogleDeepMind and the vLLM teams for immediate support.

@vllm_project: "Congrats to @GoogleDeepMind on DiffusionGemma, a 26B diffusion language model on the Gemma4 backbone, and the first dLLM natively supported in vLLM. It denoises 256-token blocks in parallel instead of generating one token at a time, achieving over 1200 output tokens per second at batch size 1 on a single H200 with FP8 precision."

Built on model runner v2's ModelState and the existing speculative decoding path, with minimal scheduler or runner changes. FP8 and NVFP4 checkpoints are available on the @RedHat_AI hub. Thanks to the @GoogleDeepMind, @RedHat_AI, and @NVIDIAAI teams!
